(* Beginning of Notebook Content *)
Notebook[{
Cell["\<\
Build a Large Language Model from Scratch \[LongDash] in Wolfram Language\
\>", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"ec78c81e-8ccb-44e9-a3b2-78f8618dc957"],

Cell["Part 8: An interactive chat widget", "Subtitle",ExpressionUUID->"5ec303f1-fde9-47df-acd1-710024d7075a"],

Cell["\<\
We close the series with the artefact every reader actually wants: a chat \
interface, inside the notebook, talking to the model we built. An input \
field, a transcript pane, a streaming generator. The model is the one Parts 1\
\[Dash]7 produced. Drop the widget cell into a notebook, evaluate it, type, \
get a reply.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c3e1f905-9d0e-403b-ab20-3a9477a8446a"],

Cell["1.  Setup", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"fab266a5-3dda-4e2e-b4b4-98f00495ca44"],

Cell["SetDirectory[NotebookDirectory[]]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"b1a565bc-3ad4-4f5d-a987-bb9392717abb"],

Cell["\<\
Get[\"../../part-01-tokeniser-and-embeddings/src/Tokeniser.wl\"]
Get[\"../../part-02-self-attention/src/Attention.wl\"]
Get[\"../../part-03-transformer-block/src/Transformer.wl\"]
Get[\"../../part-04-pretraining/src/Training.wl\"]
Get[\"../../part-05-sampling/src/Sampling.wl\"]
Get[\"../../part-06-supervised-fine-tuning/src/SFT.wl\"]
Get[\"src/Chat.wl\"]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"60a0d499-6616-41fd-adf2-758e049e0df0"],

Cell["2.  Load the post-trained model", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"7dfcdbab-845e-47d0-8560-7a03855dfe67"],

Cell["\<\
For the demo we use the small pretrained checkpoint from Part 4 (in a real \
run you'd load the GRPO-post-trained checkpoint from Part 7).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ec27e805-b462-449f-8f87-e768613f347b"],

Cell["\<\
bpe = Import[\"../../part-01-tokeniser-and-embeddings/data/bpe_trained.mx\"];
baseVocab = LLMAtoZ`Tokeniser`buildBPEVocabulary[bpe];
chatVocab = LLMAtoZ`SFT`extendVocabulary[baseVocab];
tokId  = AssociationThread[chatVocab -> Range[Length[chatVocab]]];
idTok  = AssociationThread[Range[Length[chatVocab]] -> chatVocab];
pretrained = Import[
  \"../../part-04-pretraining/data/tiny_gpt_trained.wlnet\"];
net = LLMAtoZ`SFT`expandModelVocabulary[pretrained, Length[chatVocab]];\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"280ff932-c491-4f5e-94d0-5d4384d17133"],

Cell["3.  The chat widget", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"cd8d5f17-30f2-4eab-a5be-7b2f0de0c113"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Drop the cell below into the notebook and evaluate it. The widget ",
 "is a ",
 StyleBox["DynamicModule",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " holding a running transcript, an input field, and Send / Reset ",
 "buttons. Each Send triggers ",
 StyleBox["chatTurn",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ", which formats the existing transcript and the new user message ",
 "in the SFT chat template, runs the model autoregressively until ",
 "<|eot|> or the max-tokens limit, and appends the assistant turn."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"598c0da3-21e2-4add-b789-d1ff610453a4"],

Cell["\<\
LLMAtoZ`Chat`chatWidget[net, bpe[\"MergeRules\"], tokId, idTok,
  \"MaxNew\" -> 60, \"Temperature\" -> 0.8, \"TopK\" -> 40]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"494dae4b-bd82-4f02-bd44-4c5c41043a8b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Caveat: this 1M-parameter model is laughably small. Even with the ",
 "SFT step from Part 6 and the GRPO step from Part 7 stacked on top, ",
 "it will not pass a Turing test \[LongDash] but it ",
 StyleBox["will",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " produce coherent Shakespeare-like exchanges, and every detail of ",
 "the pipeline from BPE through GRPO is something you wrote (and ",
 "could change). That is the point of the series."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"61c60d06-992a-429e-998b-cf6ebc467cc0"],

Cell["4.  Streaming generation", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"b87064cc-e505-457c-baa6-5d2aaefa450e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For watching tokens land in real time, ",
 StyleBox["streamChatTurn",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " takes a callback that fires on every emitted token. The notebook ",
 "front end can use this to update a Dynamic in place."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4e379396-cc28-4ab1-a08f-21e560e3490a"],

Cell["\<\
DynamicModule[{streamed = \"\"},
  Column[{
    Style[\"Streaming demo\", Bold, 14],
    Dynamic[Pane[streamed, {500, 100}, Scrollbars -> True]],
    Button[\"start\",
      streamed = \"\";
      LLMAtoZ`Chat`streamChatTurn[net, {}, \"Hello\",
        bpe[\"MergeRules\"], tokId, idTok,
        Function[t, streamed = streamed <> t],
        \"MaxNew\" -> 40, \"Temperature\" -> 0.7]
    ]
  }]
]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"0e56f236-abe1-4923-9438-bfc50e110d1b"],

Cell["5.  Deploying the chat as a web service", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"c7bed4db-5705-453a-8549-769112dc4186"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The same chat function can be deployed to the Wolfram Cloud and ",
 "given a permanent URL. With ",
 StyleBox["CloudConnect",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " set up:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"128b84eb-7193-4b70-a388-884850fb79f4"],

Cell["\<\
(* CloudConnect[\"you@example.com\"];
   CloudDeploy[
     APIFunction[
       {\"message\" -> \"String\"},
       LLMAtoZ`Chat`chatTurn[net, {}, #message,
         bpe[\"MergeRules\"], tokId, idTok][[-1, \"content\"]] &
     ],
     Permissions -> \"Public\"
   ]
*)\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"7ea21242-cd55-490f-ab4f-f95c85edda14"],

Cell["6.  Where we end", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"b336166a-4c9d-4690-b094-63a66e04752f"],

Cell["\<\
Across eight notebooks we built, from scratch in Wolfram Language:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"809c8510-beb7-44b9-83f2-e0baa7d20709"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "1. A byte-pair-encoding tokeniser + embedder.\n",
 "2. Single-head and multi-head causal self-attention, with the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "/", 
   SqrtBox[
    SubscriptBox["d", "k"]]}]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"ceddb49e-06c5-4133-a34c-b66ebf9fb244"],
 " factor derived rather than asserted.\n",
 "3. The full pre-norm transformer block + a closed-form parameter ",
 "count, with three reference model sizes.\n",
 "4. Pre-training on Tiny Shakespeare, with the cloud path for ",
 "scaling on a real corpus.\n",
 "5. Five sampling strategies plus speculative decoding.\n",
 "6. Supervised fine-tuning on instruction-following data.\n",
 "7. GRPO reinforcement learning post-training on a verifiable task.\n",
 "8. An interactive chat widget. This notebook."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"37ae71e2-80c8-4a4c-83b1-bbc48bcc9cc3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The final artefact, in front of you, is a small but ",
 StyleBox["functional",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " chat-style LLM where every component is something the reader can ",
 "open, change, and re-evaluate. The model is not big enough to be ",
 "useful as a product, but the pipeline is the same one production ",
 "labs use; everything in nanochat or in the Llama or GPT-2 paper has ",
 "a corresponding cell in this series."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"79bc3662-af09-40c6-bd46-492c101b1c2c"],

Cell["\<\
From here, the obvious next steps: scale (RemoteBatchSubmit on a larger \
corpus), better tokeniser (byte-level BPE matching GPT-2 exactly), better \
positional encoding (RoPE instead of learned absolute), multi-task SFT (mix \
in code, math, dialogue), reasoning-style RL (GSM8K, longer \
chains-of-thought). Every one of those is a single-package edit away.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"36f70221-62c2-4cfc-95bf-bcbbaf20d499"],

Cell["References", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"ef55acf5-1594-4dfb-9df8-d8fce75ce9b5"],

Cell["\<\
Vaswani et al. (2017). Attention Is All You Need.
Radford et al. (2019). GPT-2.
Raschka, S. (2024). Build a Large Language Model from Scratch.
Karpathy, A. (2025). nanochat.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"957e76f3-9c4c-4a3f-89bf-50b603a33f92"]
},
